# SABOTAGE: E7 (ADR-046 §6) — the erasure-completeness gate's derived-linkable coverage
# check is made a TAUTOLOGY: `bidx_covered?/2` returns `true` unconditionally instead of
# asserting a registered `:blind_index_erasure_specs` entry matches the residue's table +
# column. Every `_bidx` blind index (email_bidx / sent_to_bidx) is then reported "covered"
# even with NO tombstone arm registered — so a shredded subject's email stays confirmable
# forever via the equality oracle and the gate says nothing (the un-erasable-email_bidx
# defect ADR-046 §6 (a) closes). Flips the per-class refutability proof (with the blind-index
# arm REMOVED the email_bidx/sent_to_bidx residues must be named UNREACHED) while the
# positive control (arm present ⇒ pass) and the UNREGISTERED-`_bidx` backstop stay green.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/erasure/completeness_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: removing the blind-index arm makes the email_bidx residue UNREACHED
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/erasure/completeness.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/erasure/completeness.ex
@@ -250,10 +250,9 @@ defmodule Samen.Erasure.Completeness do
   end
 
   defp bidx_covered?(r, specs) do
-    Enum.any?(specs, fn spec ->
-      to_string(Map.get(spec, :table_name)) == r.table and
-        to_string(Map.get(spec, :bidx_column, "email_bidx")) == r.column
-    end)
+    _ = {r, specs}
+
+    true
   end
 
   # (c) storage_key — subject-linked blobs need a file spec; org-asset blobs are residual.
